<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="kicker">Your 8 weeks</span>
      <h2>What actually happens</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="arc">
      <div class="wk rv">
        <div class="n"><small>Before</small>Day 0</div>
        <div
          ><h3>Callie builds your ranges</h3><p
            >A short intake covers your goal, activity, stress, feeding season,
            and what your family actually eats. Callie reads it herself and
            approves your bands. Then your app unlocks: your ranges, your plans,
            your group, and Callie, all in one place.</p
          ></div
        >
      </div>
      <div class="wk rv">
        <div class="n"><small>Weeks</small>1–2</div>
        <div
          ><h3>Settle in, no perfection required</h3><p
            >You learn to snap plates and live inside your bands. Under range
            some days is normal. The pattern matters, not any single day, and
            Callie says so out loud.</p
          ></div
        >
      </div>
      <div class="wk rv">
        <div class="n"><small>Weeks</small>3–5</div>
        <div
          ><h3>Find your rhythm</h3><p
            >Weekly plans built around your tastes, groceries written for you,
            restaurant menus handled by your camera. Your repeat meals get
            saved, so logging takes a tap. Bad week? Log it and reset. It's
            built in.</p
          ></div
        >
      </div>
      <div class="wk rv">
        <div class="n"><small>Weeks</small>6–8</div>
        <div
          ><h3>Plate intuition takes over</h3><p
            >You start eyeballing portions and getting them right. The scale
            trends the way it should, at a pace that protects muscle and milk.
            You leave knowing how to feed yourself for good. The goal is to stop
            tracking, not track forever.</p
          ></div
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
